; The District of Columbia's estimated tax: D.C. Code § 47-4203 and
; § 47-1812.08(i), with interest at the § 47-4201(d) rate, worked through on
; Form D-2210. It is written on the shared machinery in
; returns/rules/federal/10_estimated_lib.tlisp and reproduces the Go rules in
; districtofcolumbiataxcalc/estimated.go, whose answers
; golden/testdata/estimated/DC.json.gz holds.
;
; The District's section is written on the federal pattern, but it is the
; District's own text. The prior-year test is always 110%; the threshold is
; $100; and the charge is interest at a fixed 10%, which D-2210 turns into one
; printed factor for each span between due dates, charged on each period's
; running underpayment. The figures follow the Office of Tax and Revenue's
; forms, D-40ES for 2026 and D-2210 for 2025, and the answer's divergences say
; where the D.C. Code reads otherwise. A year with no figures is answered
; ESTIMATED_OUTCOME_NO_RULES.

; One tax year's figures, as D-40ES for 2026 prints them.
(defstruct DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedYear
  (tax_year Int)
  ; Payments are needed when the tax after withholding and credits is this
  ; or more.
  (threshold Money)
  ; 90% of this year's tax and 110% of last year's, in basis points.
  (this_year_rate Int)
  (last_year_rate Int)
  ; The four due dates, before moving.
  (due_dates (Slice Date)))

(deffigures dc-estimated-2026 DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedYear 2026
  (from dc-otr-form-d40es-2026
    (threshold #usd"100.00" :at who-must-file)
    (this_year_rate 9000 :at who-must-file)
    (last_year_rate 11000 :at who-must-file)
    (due_dates [#date"2026-04-15" #date"2026-06-15" #date"2026-09-15" #date"2027-01-15"] :at when-due)))

; A tax year's rules: its figures, and what D-2210 and the D.C. Code give it.
(defstruct DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedRules
  (figures DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedYear)
  ; D-2210's exception for a balance under this share of the year's tax, in
  ; basis points.
  (remaining Int)
  ; D-2210 line 6: a quarter on each date, in basis points.
  (shares (Slice Int))
  ; § 47-1812.08(i)(4)(A) to (C): a requirement first met on or after the
  ; nth of these makes the first declaration due on the (n + 1)th due date.
  (later_groups (Slice Date))
  ; § 47-4203(c)(2)(B): interest runs no later than April 15 of the next
  ; year, the end of D-2210's fourth span.
  (stop Date)
  ; D-2210 line 10: the factor for each span, in ten-thousandths.
  (factors (Slice Int))
  ; § 47-4203(b)(2): the annualisation periods' ends.
  (period_ends (Slice Date))
  (explanation ret/EstimatedExplanation))

; How the District's estimated tax works, written by hand for the years
; these rules carry.
(= dc-estimated-explanation ret/EstimatedExplanation
  (est-explanation
    "Take your DC tax due after withholding and credits. If it is $100 or more, the District expects estimated payments. The charge for paying too little or too late is called underpayment interest. Form D-2210 figures it with a printed factor for each period."
    ["There is no interest if withholding and estimated payments reach a target. The target is the smaller of 90% of this year's DC tax or 110% of last year's. The District has no 100% tier: last year's figure is 110% at every income. The form lets you use it only if you filed a DC return for last year. Otherwise only the 90% figure counts."
     "Pay a quarter each by April 15, June 15, September 15 and the next January 15. A date on a weekend or legal holiday becomes the next business day. Withholding counts as paid evenly on the four dates. You can instead show when all of it was actually withheld. An overpayment carried from last year counts toward April. File your return and pay the balance by January 15 to skip the January payment. Interest on any earlier shortfall still runs."
     "D-2210 takes the amount still short at each due date. That counts everything required and paid so far. It is multiplied by a factor for the span to the next due date. The factors are .0175, .0265, .0351 and .0259, the last running to April 15. A payment made between due dates counts only from the next due date. The factors appear to spread the law's rate over each span's days. That rate is 10% a year compounded daily, about 10.5% a year. The law charges the actual days until payment, rounded up to the month's end. Its figure can therefore differ from the form's."
     "No interest is due if tax less withholding and estimated payments is under $100. None is due either if you had no DC tax last year and lived in DC all of it. The form also excuses a balance under 10% of the year's tax. The law doesn't mention that. The law excuses a casualty or disaster. So is someone who retired after 62 or became disabled, with reasonable cause. None of these is on D-2210, so you have to ask the Office of Tax and Revenue."]
    "The threshold is $100, not $1,000. Last year's figure is always 110%, with no income test. The charge is a fixed 10% compounded daily. The form excuses a balance under 10% of the year's tax. Its annualised method is a proration by income. Filing and paying by January 15, not January 31, replaces the last payment."
    ["D.C. Code §§ 47-4201(d), 47-4203, 47-1812.08(i)"
     "D-40ES, Estimated Payment for Individual Income Tax, 2026 (REV. 03/2026)"
     "D-2210, Underpayment of Estimated Income Tax By Individuals, 2025 (revised 05/2025)"
     "2025 D-40 booklet"]))

; The 2026 rules. No 2026 D-2210 is published, so its figures are the 2025
; form's: the 10% exception, the four quarters and the four factors, which
; are the District's fixed 10% for spans of 61, 92, 122 and 90 days, the same
; lengths in 2026. The later declaration dates, the April 15 stop and the
; annualisation periods are the D.C. Code's. A figure's source must be for
; its year, so these are written out rather than deffigures. No holiday is
; listed: the four 2026 due dates are weekdays.
(= dc-estimated-rules-2026 DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedRules
  (make-struct DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedRules
    :figures dc-estimated-2026
    :remaining 1000
    :shares [2500 2500 2500 2500]
    :later_groups [#date"2026-04-02" #date"2026-06-02" #date"2026-09-02"]
    :stop #date"2027-04-15"
    :factors [175 265 351 259]
    :period_ends [#date"2026-03-31" #date"2026-05-31" #date"2026-08-31" #date"2026-12-31"]
    :explanation dc-estimated-explanation))

(= dc-estimated-years (Table Int DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedRules)
  (table 2026 dc-estimated-rules-2026))

; "Jun 15" in the tax year, and "Jan 15, 2027" outside it.
(def dc-short-date ((d Date) (year Int)) String
  :cite ()
  (if (is (date-year d) year)
      (concat [(elt est-short-month-names (- (date-month d) 1)) " " (int-to-string (date-day d))])
      (est-short-date d)))

; D-2210's 10% exception: what is left to pay is less than the share of the
; tax.
(def dc-under-remaining ((r DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedRules) (tax Money) (left Money)) Bool
  :cite ()
  (< (* (max #usd"0.00" left) 10000) (* tax (. r 'remaining))))

; The share of the tax, rounded up to the cent, so that an amount is under
; it exactly when dc-under-remaining holds.
(def dc-remaining-limit ((r DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedRules) (tax Money)) Money
  :cite ()
  (withs (n (* (money-to-cents (max #usd"0.00" tax)) (. r 'remaining)))
    (* #usd"0.01" (/ (+ n 9999) 10000))))

(def dc-remaining-question ((r DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedRules)) ret/EstimatedQuestion
  :cite ()
  (est-ask "unsettled rule" ""
           (concat ["The form excuses a balance less than " (est-percent (. r 'remaining))
                    " of the year's tax. The law doesn't include that exception, and the figures follow the form."])))

; Which divergences change these facts' figures or answers.
(defstruct DistrictOfColumbiaAffected
  (who Bool)
  (under100 Bool)
  (prior_test Bool)
  (no_liability Bool)
  (remaining Bool)
  (list110 Bool)
  (annualised Bool)
  (factors Bool)
  (late_start Bool)
  (waiver Bool)
  (holiday Bool))

(def dc-divergence ((rule String) (form String) (form-source String) (statute String)
                    (statute-source String) (uses ret/DivergenceReading) (affects Bool))
  ret/EstimatedDivergence
  :cite ()
  (proto 'ret/EstimatedDivergence
    :rule rule :form form :form_source form-source :statute statute :statute_source statute-source
    :uses uses :affects_household affects))

; Where the Office of Tax and Revenue's forms and the D.C. Code part ways on
; a rule every District computation uses. The figures follow the forms,
; except on the 110% item in the exception list, where they follow the
; form's lines 6 to 11, which measure each installment as the statute does.
(def dc-estimated-divergences ((af DistrictOfColumbiaAffected)) (Slice ret/EstimatedDivergence)
  :cite ((law "D.C. Code" "47-4203") (law "D.C. Code" "47-1812.08") (law "D.C. Code" "47-4201"))
  [(dc-divergence "Who must make estimated payments"
     "You need payments if you expect $100 or more due after withholding and credits. The penalty form's own instructions say more than $100."
     "D-40ES (REV. 03/2026), Who must file a Form D-40ES?; 2025 D-40 booklet"
     "The test is the tax on income not subject to withholding. A declaration is needed only when it will be more than $100. Exactly $100 therefore doesn't need one."
     "D.C. Code § 47-1812.08(i)(1)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. af 'who))
   (dc-divergence "Tax under $100"
     "Take the year's tax less withholding and estimated payments. Under $100 means no interest, with no condition that the payments were on time. The front of the form counts only withholding and credits."
     "D-2210 (05/2025), front, item A, and instructions, Are there any exceptions"
     "Take the tax less credits and estimated payments that were timely made. No interest is due when that is under $100."
     "D.C. Code § 47-4203(e)(1)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. af 'under100))
   (dc-divergence "The prior-year test"
     "110% of last year's tax is open only if you filed a DC return. You must also have lived in DC all of last year."
     "D-2210 (05/2025), front, item B, and instructions for lines 4 and 5; D-40ES (REV. 03/2026)"
     "The test is 110% of the tax on last year's return. It needs a return consisting of 12 months, with no condition of residence."
     "D.C. Code § 47-4203(b)(1)(B)(ii)(II)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. af 'prior_test))
   (dc-divergence "No liability last year"
     "No interest if you had no DC tax liability last year. You must also have lived in DC the entire 12 months of it."
     "D-2210 (05/2025), instructions, Are there any exceptions"
     "No interest if last year had no tax liability, with no condition of residence."
     "D.C. Code § 47-4203(e)(2)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. af 'no_liability))
   (dc-divergence "A balance under 10% of the year's tax"
     "Take the tax left after credits, estimated payments and withholding. There's no interest if it is less than 10% of the year's DC tax, whenever paid."
     "D-2210 (05/2025), instructions, Are there any exceptions"
     "There's no such exception. Interest is excused only in the five cases the law lists."
     "D.C. Code § 47-4203(e)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. af 'remaining))
   (dc-divergence "The 110% item in the exception list"
     "The form's list of exceptions has an item for 110% of last year's tax. It excuses interest once estimated payments and withholding reach that amount. The item is listed without saying by when."
     "D-2210 (05/2025), front, item B, instructions, Are there any exceptions, and lines 6 to 11"
     "Each installment is 25% of the lesser of two figures. They are 90% of this year's tax and 110% of last year's. An installment is short by whatever wasn't paid by its due date. The form's lines for each period measure it the same way."
     "D.C. Code § 47-4203(b)(1)(B), (c)(2)(A)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_STATUTE (. af 'list110))
   (dc-divergence "The annualised income method"
     "Each period's share of the required payment is a proration. It is the income to that period over the year's income."
     "D-2210 (05/2025), instructions for line 7"
     "The law uses 22.5%, 45%, 67.5% and 90% of the tax on annualised income. Income is annualised for the first 3, 5 and 8 months and the year. A part-year return can't use it except under regulations."
     "D.C. Code § 47-4203(b)(2)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. af 'annualised))
   (dc-divergence "The interest factors"
     "The form prints a factor for the whole span to the next due date. Each period's running underpayment on its due date is multiplied by it. The factors are .0175, .0265, .0351 and .0259. A payment during a span counts only from the next due date."
     "D-2210 (05/2025), lines 8 to 11"
     "Interest is 10% a year compounded daily, on each installment's underpayment. It runs from the due date until paid or Apr 15 of the next year. A payment during a month is treated as made at the end of that month."
     "D.C. Code §§ 47-4201(d)(2), 47-4203(c)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. af 'factors))
   (dc-divergence "A requirement first met after Apr 1"
     "A quarter of the year's amount is due on each of the four dates. That holds whenever the requirement arose."
     "D-2210 (05/2025), lines 6 and 7"
     "The installments fall on the declaration dates. If first met after Apr 1, Jun 1 or Sep 1, those are Jun 15, Sep 15 or Jan 15. The law doesn't say how the installments are then sized."
     "D.C. Code §§ 47-4203(a), 47-1812.08(i)(4)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. af 'late_start))
   (dc-divergence "Retirement, disability, casualty and death"
     "The form lists no waiver for retirement, disability or a casualty. Nor does it list one for the taxpayer's death."
     "D-2210 (05/2025), instructions, Are there any exceptions"
     "The Mayor can find you retired after 62 or became disabled this year or last. With reasonable cause, there is then no interest. None is due if a casualty, disaster or other unusual event makes it inequitable. There is none for the year of death."
     "D.C. Code § 47-4203(e)(3) to (5)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. af 'waiver))
   (dc-divergence "Due dates on a weekend or holiday"
     "A voucher due on a weekend or legal holiday is due the next business day. The form doesn't say which holidays count. No 2026 due date moves."
     "D-40ES (REV. 03/2026), When are your vouchers due?"
     "The declaration is due by Apr 15, Jun 15, Sep 15 or Jan 15 of the next year. There is no rule for a weekend or holiday."
     "D.C. Code § 47-1812.08(i)(4)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. af 'holiday))])

; Which of D-2210's exceptions excuses the year once the estimated payments
; made by the fourth due date are counted: 0 none, 1 the $100, 2 the 10%.
(def dc-excuse ((f EstFacts) (r DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedRules) (exempt Bool) (dues (Slice Date))) Int
  :cite ((doc "dc-otr-form-d2210-2025" "exceptions"))
  (if (or (not (. f 'tax_known)) exempt)
      0
      (withs (fourth (elt dues 3)
              paid (+ (. f 'withheld)
                      (sum (fn ((c EstCredit)) Money (if (<= (. c 'on) fourth) (. c 'amount) #usd"0.00")) (. f 'payments)))
              left (max #usd"0.00" (- (. f 'tax) paid)))
        (if (< left (. (. r 'figures) 'threshold)) 1
            (dc-under-remaining r (. f 'tax) left) 2
            0))))

; The requirement, the due dates, each instalment's own amount, and what the
; requirement reports.
(defstruct DistrictOfColumbiaAssessment
  (req EstRequirement)
  (exempt Bool)
  ; Item A: an exception for tax under $100 applies.
  (under_threshold Bool)
  (annualised Bool)
  ; A return filed with the balance paid by the fourth due date.
  (excused_january Bool)
  ; Which exception excuses the year once payments are counted.
  (excuse Int)
  (dues (Slice Date))
  (installments (Slice Money))
  (ledger (Slice EstLedgerEntry))
  (questions (Slice ret/EstimatedQuestion))
  (divergences (Slice ret/EstimatedDivergence)))

; D-2210's proration under the annualised method: the required annual
; payment times the income to each period's end over the year's income,
; rounded half up, never less than the period before, and the whole of it by
; the year's end. Without income for the year, the regular quarters.
(def dc-annualise ((target Money) (periods (Slice ret/EstimatedTaxInputs.CallerEstimate.PeriodTax)) (regular (Slice Money)))
  (Slice Money)
  :cite ((doc "dc-otr-form-d2210-2025" "annualized-income"))
  (withs (total (. (elt periods (- (len periods) 1)) 'income)
          last (- (len periods) 1))
    (if (<= total #usd"0.00")
        regular
        (est-increments
          (fold (fn ((acc (Slice Money)) (i Int)) (Slice Money)
                  (withs (prev (if (empty? acc) #usd"0.00" (elt acc (- (len acc) 1)))
                          share (min (max (. (elt periods i) 'income) #usd"0.00") total)
                          part (round-cents (/ (* target (money-to-cents share)) (money-to-cents total))))
                    (append acc [(if (is i last) target (max prev part))])))
                ((inst empty-slice Money))
                (est-range (len periods)))))))

(def dc-estimated-assess ((inputs ret/ReturnInputs) (f EstFacts) (r DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedRules))
  DistrictOfColumbiaAssessment
  :cite ((law "D.C. Code" "47-4203" "(b)(1)(B)") (law "D.C. Code" "47-4203" "(e)")
         (law "D.C. Code" "47-1812.08" "(i)(4)")
         (doc "dc-otr-form-d40es-2026" "who-must-file") (doc "dc-otr-form-d40es-2026" "when-due")
         (doc "dc-otr-form-d2210-2025" "exceptions"))
  (withs (y (. r 'figures)
          year (. f 'tax_year)
          year-s (int-to-string year)
          last-s (int-to-string (- year 1))
          none ((inst empty-slice ret/EstimatedQuestion))
          dues (est-move-dates (. y 'due_dates) ((inst empty-slice Date)))
          known (. f 'tax_known)
          tax (. f 'tax)
          withheld (. f 'withheld)
          threshold (. y 'threshold)
          p (. f 'prior)
          has-prior (. p 'on_record)
          status (. p 'status)
          filed (est-prior-filed p)
          not-required (is status 'ret/EstimatedTaxInputs.PRIOR_RETURN_NOT_REQUIRED)
          full-year (is status 'ret/EstimatedTaxInputs.PRIOR_RETURN_FULL_YEAR)
          prior-tax (. p 'tax)
          answered (. p 'resident_answered)
          resident (. p 'resident)
          this-rate (. y 'this_year_rate)
          last-rate (. y 'last_year_rate)
          ; D-2210 lines 1 and 2: 90% of this year's tax.
          this-amount (est-rate-of this-rate tax)
          this-option (if known
                          (est-this-year-option this-rate this-amount "D-2210 (05/2025), lines 1 and 2")
                          (est-unavailable (est-this-year-option this-rate #usd"0.00" "D-2210 (05/2025), lines 1 and 2")
                                           est-needs-this-year-tax))
          ; D-2210 lines 3 and 4: 110% of last year's tax, for a filer who
          ; filed and lived in DC all year.
          closed (fn ((why String)) ret/EstimatedTargetOption
                   (est-unavailable (est-last-year-option last-rate #usd"0.00" "D-2210 (05/2025), lines 3 and 4") why))
          prior-option (if (not has-prior)
                           (closed (concat ["Needs your " last-s " DC return"]))
                           (or not-required (not filed))
                           (closed (concat ["You didn't file a " last-s " DC return"]))
                           (not full-year)
                           (closed (concat ["Your " last-s " return covered less than 12 months, not 12"]))
                           (not answered)
                           (closed (concat ["Needs whether you lived in DC all of " last-s]))
                           (not resident)
                           (closed (concat ["You didn't live in DC all of " last-s]))
                           (est-last-year-option last-rate (est-rate-of last-rate prior-tax) "D-2210 (05/2025), lines 3 and 4"))
          prior-open (is (. prior-option 'status) 'ret/OPTION_STATUS_AVAILABLE)
          prior-amount (. prior-option 'amount)
          use-prior (and prior-open (or (not known) (< prior-amount this-amount)))
          chosen-id (if use-prior (. prior-option 'id) (. this-option 'id))
          target (if use-prior prior-amount this-amount)
          options [this-option prior-option]
          ; No liability last year, for a filer who lived in DC all of it.
          no-liability (and has-prior (or full-year not-required) (or (and filed (is prior-tax #usd"0.00")) not-required))
          residence-clauses
            (append (if (and has-prior filed (not not-required) full-year (not answered))
                        [(concat ["the " (est-percent last-rate) " option is open"])]
                        ((inst empty-slice String)))
                    (if (and no-liability (not answered))
                        ["having no DC tax that year excuses you"]
                        ((inst empty-slice String))))
          residence-questions
            (if (empty? residence-clauses)
                none
                [(est-ask "residency" (concat ["Did you live in DC all of " last-s "?"])
                          (concat ["Your answer decides whether "
                                   (fold (fn ((acc String) (c String)) String
                                           (if (is acc "") c (concat [acc ". It also decides whether " c])))
                                         "" residence-clauses)
                                   "."]))])
          left (- tax withheld)
          no-liability-exempt (and no-liability answered resident)
          remaining-exempt (and (not no-liability-exempt) known (>= left threshold) (dc-under-remaining r tax left))
          req (if no-liability-exempt
                  (est-exempt options
                    (est-exception "exception-no-dc-tax-last-year" "No DC tax last year"
                                   "D-2210 (05/2025), instructions, Are there any exceptions; D.C. Code § 47-4203(e)(2)")
                    (concat ["You had no DC tax for " last-s " and lived in DC all of it. No estimated payments are needed for " year-s "."]))
                  (and (not known) (not prior-open))
                  (est-no-target options
                    (concat ["No " last-s " DC return sets a target. There is none until your " year-s " DC tax is figured."]))
                  (and (not known) (>= withheld target))
                  (est-choose options chosen-id false
                    (concat ["Your withholding of " (est-whole withheld) " covers " (est-percent last-rate) " of your " last-s
                             " DC tax, " (est-whole target) ". No estimated payments are needed, whatever your " year-s
                             " tax turns out to be."]))
                  (not known)
                  (est-choose options chosen-id true
                    (concat ["Your target is " (est-percent last-rate) " of your " last-s " DC tax, " (est-whole target)
                             ". It keeps you clear of interest whatever your " year-s " tax turns out to be. After "
                             (est-whole withheld) " of withholding, that's " (est-whole (- target withheld))
                             " of estimated payments. Pay a quarter by each date."]))
                  (< left threshold)
                  (est-exempt options
                    (est-exception-below "exception-under-threshold" "Tax less withholding" threshold
                                         "D-40ES (REV. 03/2026); D-2210 (05/2025), front, item A")
                    (concat ["Your DC tax is " (est-whole tax) ", and " (est-whole withheld) " is withheld. That "
                             (est-leaves left) (if (< tax withheld) "" (concat [", under " (est-whole threshold)]))
                             ". No estimated payments are needed."]))
                  remaining-exempt
                  (est-exempt options
                    (est-exception-below "exception-under-remaining" "Tax less withholding" (dc-remaining-limit r tax)
                                         "D-2210 (05/2025), instructions, Are there any exceptions")
                    (concat ["Your withholding of " (est-whole withheld) " leaves " (est-whole left) " of your "
                             (est-whole tax) " of DC tax to pay. That is less than " (est-percent (. r 'remaining))
                             " of it, so no interest is charged. No estimated payments are needed."]))
                  (>= withheld target)
                  (est-choose options chosen-id false
                    (concat ["Your DC withholding of " (est-whole withheld) " covers the " (est-whole target)
                             " needed for the year. No estimated payments are needed."]))
                  (est-choose options chosen-id true
                    (concat ["Your DC tax is " (est-whole tax) ", and " (est-whole withheld) " is withheld. That leaves "
                             (est-whole left) ", which is " (est-whole threshold) " or more. You need "
                             (est-whole (- target withheld)) " of estimated payments to reach your "
                             (est-whole target) " target. Pay a quarter by each date."])))
          exempt (is (. req 'status) 'ret/REQUIREMENT_STATUS_EXEMPT)
          under-threshold (and exempt (not no-liability-exempt) (not remaining-exempt))
          case-questions (if remaining-exempt [(dc-remaining-question r)] none)
          target-questions
            (append
              (if (and (not exempt) (not has-prior))
                  [(est-ask "prior year return" (concat ["Did you file a " last-s " DC return, and what was its tax?"])
                            (concat ["With it, " (est-percent last-rate) " of last year's tax may be a lower target than "
                                     (est-percent this-rate) " of this year's."]))]
                  none)
              (if (and (not exempt) (not known))
                  [(est-ask "this year's tax" (concat ["What do you expect your " year-s " DC tax to be?"])
                            (concat ["Until then, "
                                     (if (est-target-known req) "your target can only come from last year's tax" "there's no target")
                                     ". Whether the " (est-whole threshold) " and " (est-percent (. r 'remaining))
                                     " exceptions apply stays open."]))]
                  none))
          regular (est-increments (est-cumulative (. req 'target) (. r 'shares)))
          periods (. f 'periods)
          annualised (and (not (empty? periods)) (not exempt))
          annualise-questions
            (if annualised
                [(est-ask "unsettled rule" ""
                          "The form spreads your required payment by the income earned to each period. The figures use it, not the law's 22.5%, 45%, 67.5% and 90% of annualised tax.")]
                none)
          installments (if exempt
                           (map (fn ((d Date)) Money #usd"0.00") dues)
                           annualised
                           (dc-annualise (. req 'target) periods regular)
                           regular)
          ; § 47-1812.08(i)(4): the group a late requirement falls in.
          met (. inputs 'estimated_tax.requirement_first_met)
          met-set (has? (. inputs 'estimated_tax) 'requirement_first_met)
          groups (. r 'later_groups)
          late-at (fold (fn ((acc Int) (i Int)) Int (if (>= met (elt groups i)) i acc)) -1 (est-range (len groups)))
          late-start (and met-set (not exempt) (>= late-at 0))
          late-questions
            (if late-start
                [(est-ask "unsettled rule" ""
                          (concat ["First needing to pay on " (dc-short-date met year) " makes your first payment due "
                                   (dc-short-date (elt dues (+ late-at 1)) year)
                                   ". The law doesn't say how much; the figures charge a quarter on all four dates."]))]
                none)
          ; A return filed with the balance paid by January 15 takes the place
          ; of the fourth payment; it doesn't excuse an earlier shortfall.
          excused-january (and (not exempt) (. f 'return_filed_set) (<= (. f 'return_filed) (elt dues 3)))
          ledger (est-apply dues installments (est-credits f dues (. r 'shares)))
          excuse (if (est-target-known req) (dc-excuse f r exempt dues) 0)
          any-short (and (est-target-known req) (not exempt)
                         (some (fn ((e EstLedgerEntry)) Bool (> (. e 'shortfall) #usd"0.00")) ledger))
          paid (+ withheld (sum (fn ((c EstCredit)) Money (. c 'amount)) (. f 'payments)))
          w (. f 'waiver)
          claimed (and (. f 'waiver_answered)
                       (!= (. w 'cause) 'ret/EstimatedTaxInputs.WAIVER_CAUSE_NONE)
                       (!= (. w 'cause) 'ret/EstimatedTaxInputs.WAIVER_CAUSE_UNSPECIFIED))
          factors (and any-short (is excuse 0))
          af (make-struct DistrictOfColumbiaAffected
               :who (and (not exempt) known (is left threshold))
               :under100 (and any-short (is excuse 1))
               :prior_test (and (not exempt) has-prior filed full-year answered (not resident)
                                (or (not known) (< (est-rate-of last-rate prior-tax) this-amount)))
               :no_liability (and no-liability answered (not resident))
               :remaining (or remaining-exempt (is excuse 2))
               :list110 (and any-short prior-open (>= paid prior-amount))
               :annualised annualised
               :factors factors
               :late_start late-start
               :waiver (and factors claimed)
               :holiday false))
    (make-struct DistrictOfColumbiaAssessment
      :req req
      :exempt exempt
      :under_threshold under-threshold
      :annualised annualised
      :excused_january excused-january
      :excuse excuse
      :dues dues
      :installments installments
      :ledger ledger
      :questions (fold (fn ((acc (Slice ret/EstimatedQuestion)) (qs (Slice ret/EstimatedQuestion))) (Slice ret/EstimatedQuestion)
                         (append acc qs))
                       none
                       [residence-questions case-questions target-questions annualise-questions late-questions])
      :divergences (dc-estimated-divergences af))))

; Each instalment's running totals, excused where a return filed by January
; 15 replaces the fourth, or where an exception excuses the year.
(def dc-estimated-schedule ((a DistrictOfColumbiaAssessment)) (Slice ret/EstimatedInstallment)
  :cite ()
  (map (fn ((i Int)) ret/EstimatedInstallment
         (withs (e (elt (. a 'ledger) i))
           (est-installment (+ i 1) (. e 'due) (. e 'needed_by) (. e 'credited_by) (. e 'shortfall)
                            (or (!= (. a 'excuse) 0) (and (. a 'excused_january) (is i 3))))))
       (est-range (len (. a 'ledger)))))

; The penalty, its lines, and the questions it asks.
(defstruct DistrictOfColumbiaPenalty
  (penalty ret/EstimatedPenalty)
  (lines (Slice EstLine))
  (questions (Slice ret/EstimatedQuestion)))

; The interest to as_of, as D-2210 lines 7 to 12 figure it: each period's
; running underpayment, required less paid by its due date, times the
; factor for the span to the next due date or April 15, each charge in whole
; dollars; a span still running at as_of is charged its share of the factor
; by days. Without this year's tax it is figured against last year's option
; alone, so it can only be too high.
(def dc-estimated-penalty ((f EstFacts) (r DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedRules) (a DistrictOfColumbiaAssessment))
  DistrictOfColumbiaPenalty
  :cite ((law "D.C. Code" "47-4203" "(c)") (law "D.C. Code" "47-4201" "(d)(2)")
         (doc "dc-otr-form-d2210-2025" "computation"))
  (withs (stop (min (. f 'as_of) (. r 'stop))
          none ((inst empty-slice ret/EstimatedQuestion))
          no-lines ((inst empty-slice EstLine)))
    (if (or (. a 'exempt) (!= (. a 'excuse) 0))
        (DistrictOfColumbiaPenalty (est-penalty stop (est-no-lines stop) false "" est-no-waiver) no-lines none)
        (withs (dues (. a 'dues)
                ledger (est-apply dues (. a 'installments) (est-credits f dues (. r 'shares)))
                lines (fold (fn ((acc (Slice EstLine)) (i Int)) (Slice EstLine)
                              (withs (e (elt ledger i)
                                      due (. e 'due)
                                      under (if (and (is i 3) (. a 'excused_january))
                                                #usd"0.00"
                                                (max #usd"0.00" (- (. e 'needed_by) (. e 'credited_by)))))
                                (if (or (is under #usd"0.00") (<= stop due))
                                    acc
                                    (withs (end (if (< (+ i 1) (len dues)) (elt dues (+ i 1)) (. r 'stop))
                                            to (min stop end)
                                            days (days-between due to)
                                            span (days-between due end)
                                            factor (elt (. r 'factors) i)
                                            charge (round-dollar (/ (* under (* factor days)) (* 10000 span)))
                                            part (EstPart under due to days 100000 charge
                                                          (concat ["D-2210 (05/2025), line 10: ."
                                                                   (int-to-string factor) " for the period from "
                                                                   (est-long-date due)])))
                                      (append acc [(EstLine (+ i 1) due under days [part] charge)])))))
                            no-lines
                            (est-range (len ledger)))
                penalty (est-penalty stop (EstLines lines true stop) (not (. f 'tax_known)) ""
                                     (est-standard-waiver f "The Office of Tax and Revenue" 62)))
          (DistrictOfColumbiaPenalty
            penalty
            lines
            (if (and (> (. penalty 'total) #usd"0.00") (not (. f 'waiver_answered)))
                [(est-ask "penalty waiver" "Are you asking for the interest to be waived?"
                          "It can be for retiring after 62, becoming disabled, or a casualty or disaster. The Office of Tax and Revenue decides; the interest shown is before any waiver.")]
                none))))))

; One period's column of Form D-2210, lines 7 to 11.
(defform dc-form-d2210-period
  ((i Int) (e EstLedgerEntry) (lines (Slice EstLine)))
  dcd40/FormD2210.PaymentPeriod
  :cite ((doc "dc-otr-form-d2210-2025" "computation"))
  (bind mine (keep (fn ((l EstLine)) Bool (is (. l 'number) (+ i 1))) lines))
  (set :period (+ i 1))
  (line 7 "Amount required by the period, this and earlier periods'" (. e 'needed_by) :field required_to_date)
  (line 8 "DC withholding and estimated tax paid by the period" (. e 'credited_by) :field paid_to_date)
  (line 9 "Underpayment each period: line 7 minus line 8" (clamp-zero (- line7 line8)) :field underpayment)
  (line 11 "Line 9 multiplied by line 10" (if (empty? mine) #usd"0.00" (. (elt mine 0) 'total)) :field interest))

; Form D-2210 from the figures the answer's core came from: items A and B,
; lines 1 to 6 from the requirement, and lines 7 to 12 from each period's
; running totals and the interest.
(defform dc-form-d2210
  ((f EstFacts) (a DistrictOfColumbiaAssessment) (pen DistrictOfColumbiaPenalty))
  dcd40/FormD2210
  :cite ((law "D.C. Code" "47-4203") (doc "dc-otr-form-d2210-2025" "computation"))
  (bind req (. a 'req))
  (bind known (. f 'tax_known))
  (set :tax_year (. f 'tax_year))
  (set :tax_under_threshold (or (. a 'under_threshold) (is (. a 'excuse) 1)))
  (set :payments_met_requirement
       (and (not (. a 'exempt)) (not (some (fn ((e EstLedgerEntry)) Bool (> (. e 'shortfall) #usd"0.00")) (. a 'ledger)))))
  (line 1 "DC tax liability" (if known (. f 'tax) #usd"0.00") :field current_year_tax)
  (line 2 "Multiply line 1 by 90%" (est-option-amount req 'ret/TARGET_BASIS_THIS_YEAR) :field current_year_safe_harbor_tax)
  (line 3 "Prior year DC tax liability"
        (if (is (est-option-amount req 'ret/TARGET_BASIS_LAST_YEAR) #usd"0.00") #usd"0.00" (. (. f 'prior) 'tax))
        :field prior_year_tax)
  (line 4 "Multiply line 3 by 110%" (est-option-amount req 'ret/TARGET_BASIS_LAST_YEAR) :field prior_year_safe_harbor_tax)
  (line 5 "Minimum withholding and estimated tax payment required" (. req 'target) :field required_annual_payment)
  (line 6 "Multiply line 5 by 25%" (est-rate-of 2500 line5) :field periodic_payment)
  (set :uses_annualized_income_method (. a 'annualised))
  (set :payment_periods (map (fn ((i Int)) dcd40/FormD2210.PaymentPeriod
                               (dc-form-d2210-period i (elt (. a 'ledger) i) (. pen 'lines)))
                             (est-range (len (. a 'ledger)))))
  (line 12 "Underpayment interest" (. (. pen 'penalty) 'total) :field estimated_tax_penalty))

; Why these facts can't be answered under these rules, or "".
(def dc-estimated-refusal ((f EstFacts) (r DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedRules)) String
  :cite ()
  (withs (periods (. f 'periods)
          ends (. r 'period_ends))
    (if (> (len periods) (len ends))
        (concat ["districtofcolumbiataxcalc: there are " (int-to-string (len ends)) " annualisation periods, not "
                 (int-to-string (len periods))])
        (fold (fn ((acc String) (i Int)) String
                (withs (given (. (elt periods i) 'end))
                  (if (or (!= acc "") (is given (elt ends i)))
                      acc
                      (concat ["districtofcolumbiataxcalc: annualisation period " (int-to-string (+ i 1)) " ends on "
                               (est-iso-date (elt ends i)) ", not " (est-iso-date given)]))))
              ""
              (est-range (len periods))))))

; The District's answer under one year's rules.
(def dc-estimated-answer-for ((inputs ret/ReturnInputs) (r DistrictOfColumbiaEstimatedRules)) ret/EstimatedAnswer
  :cite ((law "D.C. Code" "47-4203"))
  (withs (f (est-facts inputs "DC" (est-state-prior inputs "DC"))
          refusal (dc-estimated-refusal f r))
    (if (!= refusal "")
        (est-not-answered "DC" 'ret/ESTIMATED_OUTCOME_REFUSED refusal)
        (withs (a (dc-estimated-assess inputs f r)
                explanation (. r 'explanation))
          (if (and (. a 'annualised) (!= (len (. f 'periods)) 4) (est-target-known (. a 'req)))
              (est-not-answered "DC" 'ret/ESTIMATED_OUTCOME_REFUSED "estimated: one required amount per due date")
              (not (est-target-known (. a 'req)))
              (est-answer-unknown "DC" (. a 'req) (. f 'tax_known) (. a 'questions) (. a 'divergences) explanation)
              (withs (pen (dc-estimated-penalty f r a)
                      excuse-questions (if (is (. a 'excuse) 2) [(dc-remaining-question r)]
                                           ((inst empty-slice ret/EstimatedQuestion))))
                (proto-with
                  (est-answer "DC" (. f 'as_of) (. a 'req) (. f 'tax_known)
                    (dc-estimated-schedule a)
                    (. pen 'penalty)
                    (if (est-nothing-planned f)
                        (. pen 'penalty)
                        (. (dc-estimated-penalty (est-facts-made f) r a) 'penalty))
                    (append (. a 'questions) (append excuse-questions (. pen 'questions)))
                    (. a 'divergences)
                    explanation)
                  :dc (dc-form-d2210 f a pen))))))))

; The District's answer: no rules for a year with no figures. Farmers and
; fishermen have no rule of their own; the general rules apply.
(def district-of-columbia-estimated-answer ((inputs ret/ReturnInputs)) ret/EstimatedAnswer
  :cite ((law "D.C. Code" "47-4203"))
  (withs (year (. inputs 'tax_year)
          r (lookup dc-estimated-years year)
          problem (est-input-problem inputs))
    (if (nil? r)
        (est-no-rules "DC" year)
        (!= problem "")
        (est-not-answered "DC" (est-input-outcome inputs) problem)
        (dc-estimated-answer-for inputs r))))
